This is not to say that the technology to hunt is worthless — high-speed motors bring not only suction, but also smaller, lower noise (under the same suction), longer-term continuity. But the marketing value of the "2000.000 turn" figure is far greater than the actual use value.

** Reverse view** Some would say that the value of the technological reserve is not in the current product, but in the future in the realm of visualizing the high value added areas such as power-driven systems and medical devices that high-speed motors can use for electric cars. This logic is established, but only if it is successful in commercializing these new areas, not just "technically possible".

